### ADDITIONAL TRANSACTION SCENARIOS
### Run requests in the indicated order.

### SCENARIO A - MULTIPLE BRANCHES

### A1. Create root
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/100
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1000,
  "type": "travel"
}

### A2. Create first child
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/101
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 500,
  "type": "hotel",
  "parent_id": 100
}

### A3. Create second child
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/102
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 300,
  "type": "food",
  "parent_id": 100
}

### A4. Create grandchild
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/103
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 200,
  "type": "transport",
  "parent_id": 101
}

### A5. Expected sum: 2000
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/sum/100

### A6. Expected sum: 700
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/sum/101

### A7. Expected result: [101]
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/types/hotel


### SCENARIO B - UPDATE TRANSACTION

### B1. Create transaction
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/200
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 500,
  "type": "office"
}

### B2. Expected sum: 500
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/sum/200

### B3. Update same transaction
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/200
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 900,
  "type": "office"
}

### B4. Expected sum: 900
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/sum/200


### SCENARIO C - CIRCULAR RELATIONSHIP

### C1. Create root
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/300
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 100,
  "type": "equipment"
}

### C2. Create child
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/301
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 200,
  "type": "equipment",
  "parent_id": 300
}

### C3. Create grandchild
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/302
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 300,
  "type": "equipment",
  "parent_id": 301
}

### C4. Expected HTTP 400 - Cycle detected
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/300
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 100,
  "type": "equipment",
  "parent_id": 302
}

### C5. Expected sum: 600
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/sum/300


### SCENARIO D - INVALID REQUESTS

### D1. Expected HTTP 400 - Parent not found
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/400
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 500,
  "type": "shopping",
  "parent_id": 999999
}

### D2. Expected HTTP 400 - Blank type
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/401
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 100,
  "type": ""
}

### D3. Expected HTTP 400 - Missing amount
PUT http://localhost:8080/transactions/402
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "shopping"
}

### D4. Expected HTTP 404 - Transaction not found
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/sum/999999

### D5. Expected empty array
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/types/unknown-category
